# Airwallex Sandbox API

Base URL `https://api.sandbox.airwallex.com`, paths start with `/api/v1`.
Docs: https://www.airwallex.com/docs/api

## Auth

`POST /api/v1/authentication/login` with headers `x-client-id` and `x-api-key`,
no body. Returns a 30-minute bearer token. Cache it and reuse until
`expires_at`; never re-login per request. Send as `Authorization: Bearer <token>`.

## Conventions that cause silent bugs

- **Amounts are major units.** `100` means one hundred dollars, not one dollar.
- **`request_id` must be a fresh UUID per operation.** Reuse it only to retry
  the same operation. Reusing within 7 days returns `duplicate_request_id`.
  Transfers reject ids under 10 or over 50 chars (code `018`).
- Transfers take `transfer_currency` / `transfer_amount`. Sending
  `payment_currency` returns code `001`.
- Leave `x-api-version` **off** all FX calls, else `incorrect_version`.
- A rate is not a quote: read `rate` from a rate check, `client_rate` from a quote.
- FX quotes are single-use. Get a fresh quote per conversion.

## State machines

- Failed transfers end in **`CANCELLED`**, never `FAILED`. Read `failure_type`
  and `failure_reason`. `SENT` is in-flight, never final.
- Simulated `FAILED` auto-cancels in seconds, so branch on both `FAILED` and
  `CANCELLED` or you lose `failure_reason`.
- Declined card transactions end in `FAILED`. Keep card and transfer state
  machines separate.

## Before building a beneficiary payload

Call `POST /api/v1/beneficiaries/schema` for the target country + currency.
Fields differ per corridor. Wrap validation as
`{"beneficiary": {...}, "transfer_methods": ["LOCAL"]}` — `transfer_methods`,
not `payment_methods`.

## Other

- Rate limits: 20 req/s global, 10 per endpoint, 10 concurrent. No parallel
  bursts during a live demo.
- SWIFT payouts cost a flat fee (EUR 12.85) from the same wallet; LOCAL is free.
  Add one fee per payout when sizing a conversion.
- Deposit simulation reports `PENDING` but posts immediately. Re-read balances.
- Test card `4035501000000008`, any future expiry, any CVC.
